<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kara-Khanid Khanate</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 840–<a href="/years/1212">1212</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Qarakhanids, Karakhanids, Qarakhanid Khanate, Kara-Khanids</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kara-Khanid Khanate was a Turkic dynasty that ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-asia">Central Asia</a> from about the ninth century until 1212, the first Turkic dynasty to convert to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> in the tenth century. In 999 it took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bukhara">Bukhara</a> and ended the Samanid state, dividing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transoxiana">Transoxiana</a> with the Ghaznavids. Later split into eastern and western khanates, it became a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuks</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qara-khitai">Qara Khitai</a> before falling to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khwarazmshah">Khwarazmshahs</a>.</p></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>After Sabuktigin's death Mahmud overthrew his brother Ismail in 998, and in 999, as the Samanid state collapsed between the Ghaznavids and the <b>Qarakhanids</b>, he made himself master of Khurasan.</blockquote><a href="/empire/ghaznavid-empire">Ghaznavid Empire · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>In 1137 he defeated the Western <b>Karakhanids</b> near Khujand and annexed Fergana and Tashkent, his army swollen by 10,000 Khitans formerly subject to the Karakhanids, and went on to take Kashgar, Khotan and Beshbalik.</blockquote><a href="/empire/qara-khitai">Qara Khitai · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>Under Malik Shah I (r. 1072–1092) the empire campaigned across Syria, Anatolia, the Caucasus and Central Asia and received the submission of the <b>Karakhanids</b> of Samarkand and Kashgar.</blockquote><a href="/empire/seljuk-empire">Seljuk Empire · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>The Karluks, with the Chigils and Yagmas, later founded the <b>Kara-Khanid Khanate</b>.</blockquote><a href="/empire/uyghur-khaganate">Uyghur Khaganate · Global &amp; Regional Impact</a></li><li><blockquote>In the west, the <b>Karakhanids</b>, who ruled Kashgar and the lands around it from the 10th century, became the first Turkic dynasty to adopt Islam, and their language, close to Old Turkic, became a language of Islamic literature written in Arabic script.</blockquote><a href="/language/old-turkic">Old Turkic · Speakers &amp; Spread</a></li></ul></section>
